      <article class="article">

        <h2>Why Kiwis Move to Perth</h2>
        <p>Perth punches well above its weight when it comes to salaries. Thanks to the mining industry, tradespeople and engineers earn more in Perth than almost anywhere else in Australia. The beaches rival Sydney's, the weather is Mediterranean-perfect, and the cost of living is lower than the east coast capitals.</p>
        <p>The trade-off is isolation — Perth is the most remote major city in the world. Flights home to NZ take 6–7 hours (vs 3 from the east coast), and you're 4+ hours from Sydney or Melbourne. But Kiwis who make the move often say the higher pay and relaxed pace make it worth it.</p>

        <h2>Jobs &amp; Industries in Perth</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mining &amp; resources</strong> — Perth is the global HQ for Australian mining. FIFO (fly-in fly-out) roles in iron ore, gold, lithium, and LNG pay $100k–$200k+. Even admin and support roles in mining companies pay well.</li>
          <li><strong>Construction &amp; trades</strong> — Huge demand for electricians, plumbers, welders, and diesel mechanics. $90k–$140k. Some of the highest trade wages in the country.</li>
          <li><strong>Oil &amp; gas</strong> — Woodside, Chevron, and Santos are all Perth-based. Engineering and technical roles.</li>
          <li><strong>Healthcare</strong> — Growing hospital network. Nurses earn $75k–$95k. GP shortage means opportunities for health professionals.</li>
          <li><strong>Agriculture</strong> — WA's grain belt and pastoral stations employ many Kiwis, particularly in farm management and agri-tech.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>FIFO lifestyle:</strong> Many Perth residents work 2 weeks on / 1 week off at mine sites in the Pilbara or Goldfields. Salaries are high but the lifestyle isn't for everyone. Your family stays in Perth and you fly to site.</p>

        <h2>Cost of Living in Perth</h2>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Monthly Expense</th>
                <th>Inner City (AUD)</th>
                <th>Suburbs (AUD)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>2-bed apartment rent</td><td class="price">$2,200–$2,800</td><td class="price">$1,600–$2,200</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Groceries (couple)</td><td>$550–$700</td><td>$500–$650</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Public transport (SmartRider)</td><td>$100–$150</td><td>$130–$180</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Utilities</td><td>$200–$300</td><td>$180–$280</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Petrol (car essential)</td><td>$200–$300</td><td>$250–$400</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Perth's cost of living is comparable to Brisbane — significantly cheaper than Sydney. Combined with higher salaries, particularly in mining, Kiwis in Perth often have the best saving potential. See <a href="/moving-costs">full cost breakdown</a>.</p>

        <h2>Best Suburbs for Kiwis in Perth</h2>

        <div class="checklist-box">
          <h3>Affordable &amp; family-friendly</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Baldivis / Rockingham</strong> — Southern corridor, 40 min from CBD. Very affordable, new housing, beaches. Large Kiwi community.</li>
            <li><strong>Armadale / Byford</strong> — South-east, hills backdrop. Affordable housing, growing infrastructure. Kiwi and Pacific community.</li>
            <li><strong>Ellenbrook / The Vines</strong> — Northern suburbs. New estates, family-oriented, Swan Valley wine region nearby.</li>
            <li><strong>Butler / Clarkson</strong> — Far northern suburbs. Train line to city, affordable, coastal access.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Beach lifestyle</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Scarborough</strong> — Perth's answer to Bondi. Recently redeveloped. Great surf, restaurants, and nightlife. Popular with young Kiwis.</li>
            <li><strong>Fremantle</strong> — Historic port town. Cappuccino strip, markets, live music. Quirky, artistic vibe. Ferry to Rottnest Island.</li>
            <li><strong>Cottesloe</strong> — Premium beach suburb. Stunning sunsets over the Indian Ocean. Expensive but beautiful.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Inner city &amp; professionals</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Subiaco / Leederville</strong> — Trendy inner suburbs. Cafés, bars, close to Kings Park. Walk to the CBD.</li>
            <li><strong>Victoria Park / South Perth</strong> — Across the river from the CBD. Cafés, restaurants, skyline views. Good value for inner-city living.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Shipping from NZ to Perth</h2>
        <p>Perth is the furthest Australian port from NZ, so shipping takes longer and costs slightly more.</p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Move Size</th>
                <th>Estimated Cost (NZD)</th>
                <th>Transit Time</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Boxes only (1–10)</td><td class="price">$1,200–$2,800</td><td>3–5 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>1-bed apartment</td><td class="price">$3,500–$6,000</td><td>4–6 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>2–3 bed house</td><td class="price">$6,500–$11,000</td><td>4–6 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>4+ bed house</td><td class="price">$11,000–$17,000</td><td>5–7 weeks</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Ships typically sail from Auckland via Melbourne or Adelaide to Fremantle Port. Read our <a href="/shipping-to-australia-from-nz">NZ to Australia shipping guide</a> for the full process.</p>

        <h2>Weather in Perth</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Summer (Dec–Feb):</strong> 28–38°C, dry heat. Occasional 40°C+ days. Sea breeze ("Fremantle Doctor") cools evenings.</li>
          <li><strong>Autumn (Mar–May):</strong> 18–28°C, warm and dry. Beautiful weather.</li>
          <li><strong>Winter (Jun–Aug):</strong> 8–18°C, rainy. Perth's rainy season is similar to Auckland's.</li>
          <li><strong>Spring (Sep–Nov):</strong> 14–26°C, wildflower season. Stunning landscapes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Perth is one of the sunniest cities on Earth. If you love summer, you'll love Perth.</p>

        <h2>The Isolation Factor</h2>
        <p>Let's be honest — Perth is far from home:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Flight to Auckland: 6–7 hours</li>
          <li>Flight to Sydney: 4.5 hours</li>
          <li>Time zone: 5 hours behind NZ (making calls home tricky)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Most Kiwis in Perth adjust within 6 months and come to love the lifestyle. Direct flights to NZ run daily, and Perth's international connections are growing.</p>

